  "description": "LUYCAK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H144 La4 N8 O17 S8 2+,2(Cl1 O4 1-),5(C3 H7 N1 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 7 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 7 O neighbors; La1B (La) has 7 O neighbors; La2B (La) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.753-5.382 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.84-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C104H144La4N8O17S8·2(ClO4)·5(dmf)·2(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
